# careerbot-web — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. Every value here is required for the
# admin and recruiter areas to work; the app starts without them and fails in
# ways that look like something else, so they are documented rather than
# discovered.

# Where the API lives. In compose this is the service name, not localhost.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# THE TOKEN SIGNING KEY, AND THE ONE THAT GOES WRONG.
#
# It must be the SAME VALUE the backend signs with, where it is called
# JWT_SECRET_KEY. Two names for one secret: a compose file that feeds one env
# file to both services sets the backend's name and leaves this one empty.
#
# The symptom is not an error. Signing in SUCCEEDS, the API answers 200, the
# toast says "Login successful" -- and then every admin page redirects back to
# /admin/login, because the middleware has no key to verify the session with
# and correctly refuses to trust it. It reads like a wrong password.
#
# The middleware accepts JWT_SECRET_KEY as a fallback for exactly this reason,
# so setting either name works. Set one.
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-the-backend-JWT_SECRET_KEY
